# Reading: First Position in G (repertoire plan: st-read-first-g). An original 16-bar reading
# study in G major, first position, one finger per fret (fret 1 finger 1 ... fret 4 finger 4).
# It covers all six strings, from G on string 6 fret 3 up to G on string 1 fret 3, with F# in
# both octaves: string 4 fret 4 and string 1 fret 2.
# Bars 1-4 (strings 6-4) ask a question that ends on D; bars 5-8 answer it and come home to G.
# Bars 9-12 are bars 1-4 an octave higher, on strings 3-1: the same tune, read on other strings.
# Bars 13-16 walk from the top G all the way down to the low G. Eighth notes come in pairs, on
# a beat and its "and". Every note on beats 1 and 3 belongs to the teacher's chord; the others
# are chord notes or steps between them.
